STARTER FILES - CURRENT REPOSITORY FOUNDATION

AGENTS.md
Project-specific instructions and assumptions.

README.md
Basic project description: Vite, React, and Redux client application.

index.html
Browser entry point, metadata, favicon references, global console.logD helper, and React mount element.

index.jsx
React application entry point. Creates the React root, provides the Redux store, and renders F1.

vite.config.js
Vite configuration for React, public assets, source maps, build output, and bundle naming.

package.json
Project metadata, Node version requirement, npm scripts, and runtime/build dependencies.

package-lock.json
Exact dependency and transitive-dependency versions installed by npm.

.gitattributes
Git LFS configuration for large image assets.

.gitignore
Ignored build output, private files, dependencies, and generated files.

.comments
Development notes describing article data properties across forms, storage, Redux, and the DOM.

CURRENT FOUNDATION
The repository currently contains the minimal Vite/React application shell. The next starter structure should likely add the F1 component, Redux store, feature components, public assets, and application styling.
